WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.529
This is Org Builder for VCF Automation,

2
00:00:03.579 --> 00:00:08.800
installing our lab catalog into a brand-new organization called acme.

3
00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:13.106
One command made acme a few minutes ago,

4
00:00:13.156 --> 00:00:18.550
empty apart from its quota, its networking and a first administrator.

5
00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:23.131
Connect takes the platform's addresses from a site file,

6
00:00:23.181 --> 00:00:27.834
and its tokens and passwords from this workstation's own files,

7
00:00:27.884 --> 00:00:29.850
so nobody types a password.

8
00:00:30.250 --> 00:00:34.100
VCF Automation, vCenter and NSX: all signed in.

9
00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:38.480
Discover only reads, and it takes about seven seconds.

10
00:00:44.500 --> 00:00:49.572
The result: a working platform, and an organization with nothing in it yet.

11
00:00:49.622 --> 00:00:52.850
No images, no catalog items, no binaries server.

12
00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:05.250
The kit's big files come from a media bundle, each one checked by SHA-256.

13
00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:09.599
The install itself comes as three packages.

14
00:01:09.649 --> 00:01:13.041
The foundation sets the organization up inside:

15
00:01:13.091 --> 00:01:15.750
projects, VPCs and a content library.

16
00:01:16.150 --> 00:01:19.920
The binaries server is where the labs get their installers.

17
00:01:19.970 --> 00:01:25.100
And the nested lab catalog needs both, so one Install walks all three, in order.

18
00:01:25.500 --> 00:01:28.850
Choose fills in the new site file.

19
00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:37.607
It starts from the template, and the organization,

20
00:01:37.657 --> 00:01:42.100
its client ID and its token files come straight from the sign-in.

21
00:01:42.700 --> 00:01:47.595
Everything the platform already has is a pick-list of what Discover found,

22
00:01:47.645 --> 00:01:49.600
so there's nothing to mistype.

23
00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:54.681
For the Windows template, I pick a copy of our own from another library.

24
00:01:54.731 --> 00:01:57.900
vCenter copies it across, so nothing is uploaded.

25
00:01:59.700 --> 00:02:02.750
And the checks run again after every choice.

26
00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:06.300
Validate runs the readiness checks.

27
00:02:09.300 --> 00:02:13.850
Anything that isn't there yet shows as "to build": the install makes it.

28
00:02:14.250 --> 00:02:19.200
Failures come first, each with the runbook step that fixes it.

29
00:02:20.500 --> 00:02:25.650
Plan writes the new file, site-acme.yaml, beside the guides.

30
00:02:26.050 --> 00:02:32.450
It's the template with the chosen values set in place, comments and all,

31
00:02:34.300 --> 00:02:36.950
and the guide's own site check reads it straight away.

32
00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:45.515
A short cut here. Off camera, the site file got its trainers,

33
00:02:45.565 --> 00:02:48.878
and the runbook steps our lab had already done,

34
00:02:48.928 --> 00:02:53.100
on this platform and this workstation, were marked as done.

35
00:02:53.500 --> 00:02:59.500
Back on Packages, everything now points at the new file, with nothing installed yet.

36
00:03:01.200 --> 00:03:04.009
One Install, up to the catalog's last item;

37
00:03:04.059 --> 00:03:07.200
the class checks and acceptance labs come later.

38
00:03:09.200 --> 00:03:12.389
It runs the same command you'd type at a console,

39
00:03:12.439 --> 00:03:14.900
so a console could carry on from here.

40
00:03:19.100 --> 00:03:21.478
Some runbook steps are still done by hand,

41
00:03:21.528 --> 00:03:24.600
so the install stops and asks, right here on the page.

42
00:03:25.000 --> 00:03:29.750
Step four point three W wants two profile IDs in the site file.

43
00:03:30.150 --> 00:03:33.550
Choose already put them there, so: Done.

44
00:03:38.900 --> 00:03:41.860
Step four point four is the directory.

45
00:03:42.260 --> 00:03:46.960
There's no Active Directory in this film, so: Skip, and the walk goes on.

46
00:03:54.560 --> 00:03:58.550
The next question waited eight minutes while I restarted the recording.

47
00:04:00.160 --> 00:04:05.870
It's the binaries server's DNS domain, a value the template leaves out: res dot lab.

48
00:04:08.960 --> 00:04:12.127
Then the long part, over an hour in fifteen seconds.

49
00:04:12.177 --> 00:04:17.510
The binaries server deploys and takes on twenty-four and a half gig of installer media.

50
00:04:17.910 --> 00:04:21.600
Then the images: the vCenter ISO alone is twelve gig,

51
00:04:21.650 --> 00:04:26.610
and VCF Automation takes another sixteen minutes to hand it to vCenter.

52
00:04:27.010 --> 00:04:30.210
Then the blueprints and the catalog items.

53
00:04:30.610 --> 00:04:36.124
And that's acme, on the page: the foundation and the binaries server installed,

54
00:04:36.174 --> 00:04:38.660
and the catalog up to its last item.

55
00:04:40.010 --> 00:04:42.508
Every component says how it went in:

56
00:04:42.558 --> 00:04:46.260
by the installer, by part of it, or by runbook steps.

57
00:04:48.510 --> 00:04:54.460
And the runbook's own record, in the Build view, stays in step with the packages.

58
00:04:57.910 --> 00:05:02.316
Here's acme in VCF Automation, signed in as its administrator,

59
00:05:02.366 --> 00:05:04.760
and again nobody typed a password.

60
00:05:11.510 --> 00:05:16.210
The catalog: nine items, released into its two projects.

61
00:05:16.810 --> 00:05:19.689
Its content library, filled by the same install:

62
00:05:19.739 --> 00:05:22.192
the kit's images uploaded from the media,

63
00:05:22.242 --> 00:05:25.060
and the Windows template copied inside vCenter.

64
00:05:31.010 --> 00:05:31.960
Its projects,

65
00:05:35.510 --> 00:05:39.810
and a VPC for each student, all named in the site file.

66
00:05:43.210 --> 00:05:47.660
And the binaries server the labs read their installers and scripts from.

67
00:05:48.110 --> 00:05:51.560
A brand-new organization, built from the kit,

68
00:05:51.610 --> 00:05:55.060
without a single click inside VCF Automation.

